    "created_at": "2019-10-14T16:31:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-14T16:31:11Z",
    "body": "@annevk Can you add the i18n-tracking label please?\r\n\r\nIn #4986 @battre mentions using a pattern string such as `[mm/yy]`. Pattern strings have the I18N disadvantage that translators have to puzzle out whether they need to translate the pattern (or not). A better mechanism used in more modern I18N APIs are \"skeletons\", which allow the locale to determine the best pattern to use to collect specific input. When this mechanism is used, translators and webdevs don't have to modify the the pattern when translating the page.\r\n\r\nHaving said that, in this case the pattern isn't locale affected, so building in a specific format makes more sense to me. ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
