    "created_at": "2019-10-15T07:50:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-10-15T07:50:49Z",
    "body": "I haven't checked the historical record, but I would guess that when designing the spec, it was hoped that web authors would ask for YYYY format to get the nice autocomplete. Maybe the spec was designed when Y2K was fresher on everyone's minds.\r\n\r\nThis doesn't seem to have happened, and so instead people are not getting autocomplete at all. So yeah, we should probably fix this.\r\n\r\nPersonally I would prefer simple tokens of the form `cc-exp-mmyy` and `cc-exp-year-yy` instead of a new microsyntax inside the autocomplete tokens using `[]`.\r\n\r\nI'll also note that we have precedent (with https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/3745#issuecomment-487101498) for very weak \"implementer interest\" signals for expanding the autofill token list, which IMO is suitable for what is largely an ecosystem coordination mechanism.",
